Ladybird reports the document’s title to the page when a title
element is inserted into a document or removed from one, and when a
connected title element’s children change. Blink does the same in
HTMLTitleElement::InsertedInto(), RemovedFrom() and ChildrenChanged(),
the last only for an element in the document tree. WebKit does it in
HTMLTitleElement::postConnectionSteps(), removingSteps() and
childrenChanged(), the last only for a connected element. And Gecko’s
HTMLTitleElement::BindToTree() and UnbindFromTree() each tell the
document of a possible title change, in SendTitleChangeEvent().
